@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Wizard Stock Market</PageTitle>

<div class="page-header centered">
    <h1>About WSM</h1>
</div>

<div class="about-container">
    <section class="about-section">
        <h2>What is Wizard Stock Market?</h2>
        <p>
            Wizard Stock Market (WSM) is a virtual stock trading simulator that allows you to buy and sell 
            shares of fictional companies using virtual currency. It's designed as an educational tool 
            to help you understand the basics of stock trading, portfolio management, and financial 
            decision-making — all without risking real money.
        </p>
        <p>
            Whether you're a student learning about finance, or simply curious about how the stock market 
            works, WSM provides a safe and engaging environment to practice trading strategies.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature-card">
                <h3>Live Market</h3>
                <p>Stock prices update in real-time with simulated market fluctuations. Watch prices rise and fall as you decide when to buy or sell.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
                <h3>Portfolio Management</h3>
                <p>Build your portfolio by purchasing shares. Track your holdings, monitor performance, and sell when the time is right.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
                <h3>Watchlist</h3>
                <p>Keep an eye on stocks you're interested in. Add them to your watchlist for quick access without committing to a purchase.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
                <h3>Bank Loans</h3>
                <p>Need extra capital? Apply for loans from virtual banks. Each bank has different rates and requirements based on your score.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Scoring System</h2>
        <div class="scoring-info">
            <div class="score-explanation">
                <p>Your score reflects your trading success and is calculated based on your total profit:</p>
                <div class="score-formula">
                    <span class="formula-label">Score</span>
                    <span class="formula-equals">=</span>
                    <span class="formula-value">1 point per £10 profit</span>
                </div>
                <ul class="score-rules">
                    <li>Score starts at <strong>0</strong> for new traders</li>
                    <li>Score increases when you sell stocks at a profit</li>
                    <li>Score decreases when you sell at a loss</li>
                    <li>Minimum score is <strong>0</strong> (cannot go negative)</li>
                    <li>A minimum score of <strong>25</strong> is required to apply for bank loans</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="score-tips">
                <h4>Tips for Success</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Buy low, sell high — watch price trends before committing</li>
                    <li>Diversify your portfolio across multiple stocks</li>
                    <li>Use the watchlist to track opportunities</li>
                    <li>Build your score before taking out loans</li>
                    <li>Review your transaction history to learn from past trades</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Technical Details</h2>
        <div class="tech-grid">
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">Framework</span>
                <span class="tech-value">ASP.NET Blazor Server</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">Runtime</span>
                <span class="tech-value">.NET 7.0</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">UI</span>
                <span class="tech-value">Razor Components</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">State</span>
                <span class="tech-value">Scoped Services</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">Styling</span>
                <span class="tech-value">Custom CSS</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tech-item">
                <span class="tech-label">Charts</span>
                <span class="tech-value">SVG Rendering</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-note">
            Stock prices are simulated using randomised algorithms that create realistic market behaviour. 
            The application uses real-time updates via SignalR for seamless price changes.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section github-section">
        <h2>Source Code</h2>
        <p>This project is open source. View the code, report issues, or contribute on GitHub:</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/Roland-02/Wizard_Stock_Market" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="github-link">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="github-icon">
